kes":"The shortage will be noticed when the final accounting is done. They're hoping they die before that happens"},"plotHooks":["They've been offered money to not ask questions about something they hadn't even started asking about.","Something they were told was destroyed is apparently not destroyed."],"influence":"low","power":2,"presentation":{"impression":"Reserved. Not hostile, just private.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Merchant Guilds","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_6","name":"Rudolf Koch","gender":"male","role":"Debt Collector","title":"Agent","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"cowardly","modifier":"cynical","tell":"makes deliberate, theatrical eye contact to assert dominance","speech":"Uses long pauses as punctuation, sits comfortably in silence"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"average height, unremarkable frame","feature":"eyes that never stop moving","clothes":"whatever was available (they don't care about dress)"},"goal":{"short":"Stay useful to the wrong people so they stay breathing.","long":"Matter to the people immediately around them: small scale, real"},"secret":{"what":"Is the illegitimate heir to a title currently held by someone who doesn't know they exist","stakes":"Could claim it, or could be seen as a threat by those who benefit from the status quo"},"plotHooks":["Someone left an item in their care and hasn't returned. The item is valuable. The absence is now suspicious.","They found something hidden in a place it shouldn't be. They put it back. They haven't told anyone."],"influence":"low","power":1,"presentation":{"impression":"Tired, but alert. The combination of someone who works hard and pays attention.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"corrupt":true,"corruptionVector":"fear","secondaryAffiliation":"Front businesses","corruptTies":{"criminalInstitution":"Front businesses","thievesGuild":"Front businesses"},"factionAffiliation":"War Council"},{"id":"npc_9","name":"Megingoz Klein","gender":"male","role":"Healer","title":"Heiler","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":"optimistic","flaw":"imperious","modifier":"ambitious","tell":"uses elaborate, florid greetings regardless of context","speech":"Uses understatement and dry humour as a defence mechanism"},"physical":{"age":"mid-thirties","build":"compact and powerful","feature":"a network of small scars on their knuckles","clothes":"travel-worn but well-maintained gear"},"goal":{"short":"Secure enough weapons reserves to outlast the blockade","long":"Survive this: everything else can wait"},"secret":{"what":"Owes Adalbero Richter a debt from before either of them held their current position: one that Adalbero Richter has never formally called in","stakes":"The silence feels like patience rather than forgiveness"},"plotHooks":["Someone is paying their soldiers more than their salary. The soldiers aren't saying who.","They received orders from above that contradict what they know to be right. They haven't acted on either yet."],"influence":"low","power":2,"presentation":{"impression":"Ordinary in a way that is itself a kind of presence.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"}],"dominantCategory":"other","powerFactionName":"Town Council","powerFactionPower":22,"powerFactionCat":"government"},{"name":"The Shield Compact","members":[{"id":"npc_1","name":"Vilbirg Werner","gender":"female","role":"Mayor","title":"Bürgermeister","category":"government","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"hypocritical","modifier":"cynical","tell":"maintains an unnervingly fixed smile during conflict","speech":"Prefaces bad news with elaborate courtesy, good news with none"},"physical":{"age":"mid-forties","build":"barrel-chested","feature":"a network of small scars on their knuckles","clothes":"expensive but conservative merchant dress"},"goal":{"short":"Restore enough perceived legitimacy to make the governing role functional, or identify an exit before the gap between title and authority becomes irreversible.","long":"Die in office having kept the peace (legacy matters more than wealth)"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["A recruit they turned away has since joined a different outfit. The different outfit is now paying them to monitor this one.","A merchant they publicly opposed is now publicly supporting them. No explanation offered."],"influence":"high","power":10,"presentation":{"impression":"Friendly and community-minded. The kind of person other residents speak well of.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Knows everyone, introduces you to people, seems like the natural first contact for newcomers."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Town Council","factionGoal":"Maintain Town Council's position against current pressure","structuralPosition":"Holds nominal governing authority where the legitimacy of that position is in active question. Formal title and real decision-making power are not the same thing.","activeConstraint":"Cannot take the action most likely to restore legitimacy without exposing the informal arrangements that currently keep governance functional.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_2","name":"Leopold Friedmann","gender":"male","role":"Guard Captain","title":"Hauptmann","category":"military","personality":{"dominant":"honest","flaw":"domineering","modifier":"detached","tell":"taps their foot in a complex rhythm when bored","speech":"Speaks in analogies and metaphors, even when clarity would serve better"},"physical":{"age":"mid-sixties","build":"imposingly tall","feature":"a cough they suppress with visible effort","clothes":"a dress uniform kept for funerals, worn thin at the elbows"},"goal":{"short":"Maintain operational cohesion and institutional loyalty while the political situation makes the chain of command ambiguous.","long":"Rebuild guard morale after years of under-funding and low prestige"},"secret":{"what":"Has been paying a health official to suppress a finding about their product","stakes":"People are being harmed; the official is growing nervous; the finding is documented"},"plotHooks":["A prisoner in their custody knows something valuable. So does someone with reason to ensure they never speak.","A weapons cache they were responsible for is smaller than it should be. They haven't reported it yet."],"influence":"high","power":9,"presentation":{"impression":"Efficient and correct in every interaction. The manner of someone following procedure.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Processes requests quickly. Doesn't ask about things that aren't their business."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Military/Guard","structuralPosition":"Commands enforcement capacity where civilian governance is failing. The military's relationship with civilian authority is under pressure.","activeConstraint":"Cannot act unilaterally to fill the governance vacuum without becoming a political actor in ways that compromise the institutional neutrality the role requires.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_4","name":"Adalbero Richter","gender":"male","role":"Garrison Commander","title":"Hauptmann","category":"military","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"cowardly","modifier":"iconoclast","tell":"takes written notes during conversations, even casual ones","speech":"Uses softening phrases that make every statement sound like a question"},"physical":{"age":"early thirties","build":"heavyset and solid","feature":"an old injury that affects their gait","clothes":"soldier's practical dress with officer's insignia"},"goal":{"short":"Maintain operational cohesion and institutional loyalty while the political situation makes the chain of command ambiguous.","long":"End this siege in a way the settlement can recover from"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["The ambush that killed two of their best people wasn't random. Someone knew the patrol route.","They are carrying out orders they believe are wrong. They have not yet decided at what point they stop carrying them out."],"influence":"high","power":10,"presentation":{"impression":"Warm, a little effusive. The first person to make you feel you've arrived somewhere safe.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Asks good questions about your journey. Remembers the answers."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Military/Guard","structuralPosition":"Commands enforcement capacity where civilian governance is failing. The military's relationship with civilian authority is under pressure.","activeConstraint":"Cannot act unilaterally to fill the governance vacuum without becoming a political actor in ways that compromise the institutional neutrality the role requires.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"}],"dominantCategory":"military","powerFactionName":"Military/Guard","powerFactionPower":23,"powerFactionCat":"military"},{"name":"The Devout Circle","members":[{"id":"npc_3","name":"Gisela Schneider","gender":"female","role":"High Priest","title":"Pfarrer","category":"religious","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"imperious","modifier":"cautious","tell":"never volunteers information, only answers what is asked","speech":"Never interrupts, waits out even the longest speaker, then answers the first point only"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"barrel-chested","feature":"eyes that never stop moving","clothes":"plain devotional dress with one opulent accessory"},"goal":{"short":"Extend the institution's civic role in ways that survive whatever governance reconsolidation follows.","long":"Unite the fractious local clergy under a single doctrinal standard"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["A donation was made to the institution under conditions the donor didn't disclose publicly. The conditions are becoming relevant.","A novice has the gift. They know what that means for the novice. They're not sure what to do."],"influence":"moderate","power":5,"presentation":{"impression":"Watchful, in a religious way: not suspicious, but as though taking a reading.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","structuralPosition":"Holds institutional religious authority in a settlement where civic governance is failing. Religious institutions often absorb civic functions when secular authority contracts.","activeConstraint":"Civic engagement that appears opportunistic risks being reversed by a reconsolidated authority that resents the encroachment.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"}],"dominantCategory":"religious","powerFactionName":"Religious Authorities","powerFactionPower":19,"powerFactionCat":"religious"}],"conflicts":[{"parties":["The Independent Bloc","The Shield Compact"],"issue":"Succession to a council seat","stakes":"Political influence","intensity":"low","desc":"The Independent Bloc and The Shield Compact are in low conflict over succession to a council s