 Economy suffers, population discontent grows.","severity":"medium"}],"summary":"✗ NOT VIABLE: 2 critical issues prevent settlement survival.","metrics":{"foodBalance":{"dailyNeed":10733,"dailyProduction":6358,"deficit":4375,"deficitPercent":41,"surplus":0,"agricultureModifier":1.5,"stressModifier":0.6},"tradeAccess":"crossroads","criticalIssueCount":2,"dependencyCount":7,"warningCount":0}},"history":{"age":63,"founding":{"age":63,"reason":"developed where herders gathered seasonally until the gathering became permanent","foundedBy":"military veterans given land grants who brought their skills with them","initialChallenge":"competition from nearby markets","overcoming":"by making enough right decisions to survive the wrong ones","stressNote":"What the founders built is now being tested by forces they could not have anticipated. The original reasons for settling here have become irrelevant to immediate survival."},"historicalEvents":[{"yearsAgo":48,"type":"occupation_infiltration","name":"The Purge","description":"Fear of hidden infiltrators (not always unfounded) bred denunciations and a climate of mistrust","severity":"major","lastingEffects":["A standing security office and informant network persist"],"plotHooks":["Evidence that survived the years indicates the agents' handler is someone in a position of trust, and the PCs have already met them","Evidence that survived the years indicates an innocent person has been identified as a spy and is about to be executed"],"templateType":"infiltration_fear","anchored":true},{"name":"The Iron Dispute","description":"Rights to the local iron deposits became the subject of a prolonged dispute between the settlement and a rival lord. The outcome shaped who controls extraction to this day.","lastingEffects":["Iron production rights still legally contested in some records","Fortified extraction sites established during the dispute"],"plotHooks":["Old deed to the iron rights has resurfaced in an estate sale","A rival family claims their ancestor was cheated out of the original mining contract"],"severity":"major","type":"economic","yearsAgo":28,"anchored":false},{"yearsAgo":26,"type":"disaster","name":"The Siege","description":"An approaching danger set the community against itself over the right response","severity":"catastrophic","lastingEffects":["A standing levy roster kept ready in the town archive"],"plotHooks":["The threat has an agent already inside the settlement","The threat is being exaggerated by someone who profits from wartime contracts"],"templateType":"external_threat"}],"currentTensions":[{"type":"resource_scarcity","description":"The supply of key goods (the settlement's economic backbone) is under pressure. Settlement cannot cover ~4375 lbs of food per day (41% of needs) and has no dependable trade route.","factions":["Hoarders","Desperate poor","Price regulators"],"lastingEffects":["Emergency granary reserves mandated by ordinance since the shortage","Price ceilings on the affected goods still enforced in lean seasons"],"plotHooks":["A warehouse full of the resource is being held off the market deliberately","The scarcity was engineered. Someone destroyed the competing supply route","An alternative source exists but the information is being suppressed"],"severity":["minor","major"],"specificIssue":"Settlement cannot cover ~4375 lbs of food per day (41% of needs) and has no dependable trade route."},{"type":"occupation_legacy","description":"A previous occupation ended, but collaborators and resisters continued to live side by side, their history unresolved","factions":["Former collaborators","Former resistance","New generation wanting to move on"],"lastingEffects":["Collaborator and resistance families still keep to separate quarters","Wartime property seizures remain legally unresolved"],"plotHooks":["A collaborator family's wartime fortune was built on betrayals that are finally surfacing","Resistance fighters kept records that would expose people still in power","A former occupier officer has returned under a false identity"],"severity":["major","catastrophic"]}],"historicalCharacter":"The Siege is the reason this settlement is here at all, in its current form, not because it was founded then, but because it was remade then, and what was remade is what we have","eventsTimeline":[{"year":15,"yearsAgo":48,"name":"The Purge","type":"occupation_infiltration","anchored":true},{"year":35,"yearsAgo":28,"name":"The Iron Dispute","type":"economic","anchored":false},{"year":37,"yearsAgo":26,"name":"The Siege","type":"disaster","anchored":false}],"legacyAnnotations":[{"annotation":"The Siege (26 years ago) created pressure that has not been fully resolved: the settlement has not fully insulated itself from the pressures that calamity revealed. The lasting consequence (a standing levy roster kept ready in the town archive) remains structurally embedded.","eventType":"disaster","yearsAgo":26,"severity":"catastrophic","eventName":"The Siege"},{"annotation":"The Iron Dispute (28 years ago) created pressure that has not been fully resolved: current economic pressure has structural antecedents. The present situation reflects dependencies established then. The lasting consequence (iron production rights still legally contested in some records) remains structurally embedded.","eventType":"economic","yearsAgo":28,"severity":"major","eventName":"The Iron Dispute"}],"siegeNarrative":"The Iron Dispute is still present in living memory: The supply of key goods (the settlement's economic backbone) is under pressure. Settlement cannot cover ~4375 lbs of food per day (41% of needs) and has no dependable trade route."},"isolationSupport":{"version":1,"applicable":false,"tier":"town","requiredCapacity":52,"capacity":52,"deficit":0,"status":"connected","paths":[],"magicDependent":false},"culturalIdentity":{"key":"germanic","label":"Germanic-inspired","scope":"A timber-and-stone, guild-and-estate design grammar.","builtForm":"Farmsteads and craft yards form 