kets. This income stays in the settlement but flows to criminal actors, not the public treasury.","isCriminal":true,"weight":10.876209677419356,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Market Taxes","percentage":13,"desc":"Market day stall fees and toll collection on goods entering the market.","weight":8.86209677419355,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Toll Revenue","percentage":11,"desc":"Passage tolls on all roads and bridges serving the crossroads position.","weight":8.056451612903226,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Entrepôt Trade","percentage":10,"desc":"Transit duties, warehouse fees, and re-export premiums from goods passing through the crossroads position.","weight":7.250806451612903,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Guild Fees","percentage":10,"desc":"Annual licensing fees and fines levied by guild oversight.","weight":7.250806451612903,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Banking Fees","percentage":8,"desc":"Interest income, currency exchange commissions, and safe deposit charges.","weight":5.639516129032258,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Church Tithes","percentage":6,"desc":"Tithes, offerings, and fees for burial and sacramental services collected by resident clergy.","weight":4.431048387096775,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Property Rents","percentage":6,"desc":"Ground rents on civic-owned buildings, stalls, and residential plots within the walls.","weight":4.028225806451613,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Fish & Preserved Produce","percentage":5,"desc":"Catch landed and sold fresh or preserved; salt fish are a major regional export commodity.","weight":3.2225806451612904,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Iron & Metalwork","percentage":5,"desc":"Local ore feeds the smithy directly. Metalwork income is not trade-route dependent.","weight":3.2225806451612904,"priorityNote":null},{"source":"Wool & Textile Trade","percentage":5,"desc":"Local flocks provide raw wool; weavers and fullers convert it to cloth sold across the region.","weight":3.2225806451612904,"priorityNote":nul