ted and durable.","institution":"Fuller"},{"name":"Furniture making","desc":"Tables, chairs, chests, beds, and cabinetry for household and commercial use.","institution":"Carpenters (5-15)"},{"name":"Gate control","desc":"Control who enters and exits. Levy tolls on goods.","institution":"Town walls"},{"name":"Glass vessels","desc":"Bottles, flasks, and cups.","institution":"Glassblower"},{"name":"Grain grinding","desc":"Grind grain into flour for bread and other foods.","institution":"Mills (2-5)"},{"name":"Hide processing","desc":"Basic tanning of animal hides into usable leather.","institution":"Tanners"},{"name":"Horse hire","desc":"Rent horses for single journeys or extended travel. Quality varies by price.","institution":"Stable district"},{"name":"Horseshoeing","desc":"Essential service for any settlement with working horses. Routine maintenance.","institution":"Blacksmiths (3-10)"},{"name":"Iron refining","desc":"Smelt raw ore into pig iron and refined ingots ready for smithing.","institution":"Smelter"},{"name":"Jewellery purchase","desc":"Rings, necklaces, brooches. Precious metalwork.","institution":"Jeweller"},{"name":"Livery and uniforms","desc":"House colours, guild uniforms, city watch livery.","institution":"Tailor's guild"},{"name":"Lumber milling","desc":"Raw logs into planks and beams. Essential input for all construction.","institution":"Sawmill (commercial)"},{"name":"Military supply","desc":"Contract supply of bows and arrows to garrison and militia. Volume pricing.","institution":"Bowyers & fletchers (guild)"},{"name":"Quality bows","desc":"Guild-certified bows meeting standardized draw weights and lengths.","institution":"Bowyers & fletchers (guild)"},{"name":"Repairs","desc":"Reforge broken tools, re-edge blades, mend ironwork. Often more valuable than new.","institution":"Blacksmiths (3-10)"},{"name":"Shoe repair","desc":"Full guild workshop. Any repair.","institution":"Cobbler's guild"},{"name":"Standard boots","desc":"Guild-certified boots. Quality-marked, price-regulated.","institution":"Cobbler's guild"},{"name":"Table wine","desc":"House wine by the jug or bottle.","institution":"Vintner"},{"name":"Tanned leather","desc":"Oak-bark tanned hides. Ready for the cobbler or saddler.","institution":"Tannery"},{"name":"Tool manufacture","desc":"Axes, ploughs, hinges, nails. The foundation of agricultural and construction work.","institution":"Blacksmiths (3-10)"},{"name":"Trade brokerage","desc":"Facilitate large commercial transactions between distant parties.","institution":"Merchant guilds (3-8)"},{"name":"Weapon smithing","desc":"Swords, spearheads, daggers. Military-grade work requires a skilled smith.","institution":"Blacksmiths (3-10)"},{"name":"Wine wholesale","desc":"Supply to taverns and inns. Contract pricing.","institution":"Vintner"},{"name":"Working clothes (bulk)","desc":"Practical clothing for soldiers and servants.","institution":"Tailor's guild"}],"magic":[],"information":[{"name":"Aurora Rationing Office","desc":"Aurora Provisioners produces Aurora Rationing Office","institution":"Aurora Provisioners","customDefinitionId":"definition:services:reference-aurora-rationing-office","customDefinitionRevisionId":"revision:services:reference-aurora-rationing-office:1","customDefinitionContentHash":"0a3e31740ff76bd00f0259d52d5a2e69801e57fe6851416f27c38a3f9573f13e","customDefinitionVersion":1,"customDefinitionFingerprint":"0a3e31740ff76bd00f0259d52d5a2e69801e57fe6851416f27c38a3f9573f13e","custom":true,"source":"custom","customDefinitionCategory":"services","localUid":"reference-aurora-rationing-office"},{"name":"Official announcements","desc":"Proclaim laws, royal decrees, and official notices to the public.","institution":"Town crier"},{"name":"Register of the dead","desc":"The sexton records who lies where. Consulted in inheritance disputes as often as in mourning.","institution":"Parish burial grounds"},{"name":"Route intelligence","desc":"Road conditions, bandit reports, toll schedules.","institution":"Caravaneer's post"}],"healing":[{"name":"Bathing","desc":"Hot and cold baths available for a small fee. Essential in cities.","institution":"Public bathhouse"},{"name":"Burial","desc":"Interment in the parish ground, with the rite that parish keeps.","institution":"Parish burial grounds"},{"name":"Grooming","desc":"Haircuts, shaving, and basic grooming services.","institution":"Public bathhouse"},{"name":"Herbal remedies","desc":"Tinctures, poultices, and dried herbs for common ailments.","institution":"Apothecary (established)"},{"name":"Life ceremonies","desc":"Births, marriages, and funerals across multiple parishes.","institution":"Parish churches (2-5)"},{"name":"Medicines and compounds","desc":"Prepared medicines for fever, pain, infection, and chronic conditions.","institution":"Apothecary (established)"},{"name":"Religious services","desc":"Multiple parishes covering different districts or communities.","institution":"Parish churches (2-5)"}],"transport":[{"name":"Caravan assembly","desc":"Register to join an outgoing caravan.","institution":"Caravaneer's post"},{"name":"Crossing fee","desc":"Collect toll from all who cross. Rate varies by load and cargo.","institution":"Toll bridge"},{"name":"Delivery contracts","desc":"Scheduled delivery runs on established routes.","institution":"Carriers' guild"},{"name":"Freight haulage","desc":"Organised road transport for goods between towns. Reliable, guild-backed.","institution":"Carriers' guild"},{"name":"Stabling","desc":"Horse care","institution":"Multiple water sources"}],"legal":[{"name":"Civic administration","desc":"Day-to-day governance of the settlement. Planning, budgeting, and dispute resolution.","institution":"Mayor and council"},{"name":"Coin appraisal","desc":"Assess weight and purity of coins. Identify clipped or debased currency.","institution":"Money changers"},{"name":"Currency exchange","desc":"Convert between different currencies at posted rates. Margin taken on each transaction.","institution":"Money changers"},{"name":"Dispute arbitration","desc":"Bring commercial and civil disputes before a magistrate.","institution":"Town hall"},{"name":"Duties and tariffs","desc":"Assessment and collection of import and export duties on all goods.","institution":"Customs house"},{"name":"Fine payment","desc":"Pay fines to secure release from detention.","institution":"Small prison/stocks"},{"name":"General trade","desc":"Agricultural produce, household goods, livestock. The economic heartbeat of the week.","institution":"Weekly market"},{"name":"Goods storage","desc":"Secure, dry storage for trade goods awaiting sale or onward shipment.","institution":"Merchant warehouses"},{"name":"Grain storage","desc":"Municipal grain reserves. Buffers the settlement against poor harvests.","institution":"Town granary"},{"name":"Holding cells","desc":"Short-term detention pending trial or payment of fines.","institution":"Small prison/stocks"},{"name":"Jewellery appraisal","desc":"Valuation for insurance, sale, or inheritance.","institution":"Jeweller"},{"name":"Livestock auction","desc":"Major livestock sales. Breeding stock, draft animals, slaughter cattle.","institution":"Annual fair"},{"name":"Permit applications","desc":"Apply for construction, business, and trade permits.","institution":"Town hall"},{"name":"Public punishment","desc":"Stocks and pillory for public shaming and minor offenses.","institution":"Small prison/stocks"},{"name":"Quality certification","desc":"Guild mark indicating goods meet agreed standards.","institution":"Craft guilds (5-15)"},{"name":"Seasonal trading","desc":"Once-a-year market drawing merchants from across the region.","institution":"Annual fair"},{"name":"Trade licensing","desc":"Issue permits for market stalls, new businesses, and regulated trades.","institution":"Mayor and council"},{"name":"Weekly market","desc":"Regular market days with produce, goods, and livestock.","institution":"Market square"}],"employment":[{"name":"Apprenticeship programs","desc":"Formal training under a master craftsperson. Multi-year commitment.","institution":"Craft guilds (5-15)"},{"name":"Hiring hall","desc":"Workers, mercenaries, guides available","institution":"Housing (180-1000 structures)"},{"name":"Laborer hire","desc":"Unskilled and semi-skilled laborers for day work.","institution":"Hireling hall"},{"name":"Night patrol","desc":"Patrol the streets after dark. Deter crime and respond to incidents.","institution":"Town watch"}],"entertainment":[{"name":"Cold reading","desc":"Convincing but fraudulent personality readings.","institution":"Charlatan fortune tellers"},{"name":"Companionship","desc":"Paid companionship services.","institution":"Brothel"},{"name":"Entertainment","desc":"Music, games, storytelling every night","institution":"Housing (180-1000 structures)"},{"name":"Private entertainment","desc":"Hire the troupe for private events and festivals.","institution":"Traveling performers"},{"name":"Private rooms","desc":"Secure, discreet rooms for meetings requiring privacy.","institution":"Brothel"},{"name":"Public performance","desc":"Street and square performances: juggling, music, comedy, acrobatics.","institution":"Traveling performers"}],"criminal":[{"name":"Muscle for hire","desc":"Rough up a target, intimidate a debtor, move a problem: informal, no contract.","institution":"(street gang)"},{"name":"Petty crime","desc":"Pickpocketing, muggings, and opportunistic theft in their territory.","institution":"Street gang"},{"name":"Protection racket","desc":"Pay or have your premises damaged. The gangs are territorial and consistent.","institution":"(street gang)"},{"name":"Untaxed storage","desc":"Hold goods in dug caches off the rolls.","institution":"Underground network"}]},"powerStructure":{"factions":[{"faction":"Military/Guard","power":23,"desc":"Town watch and militia; enforce ordinances, manage disorder, and report to the council. Behind the governing council by enough margin that direct challenge is not viable: they route their influence through procedure, not confrontation. They outmatch the guild institutionally, which keeps the criminal operation suppressed rather than eliminated. There is a difference. They and the religious authorities operate parallel systems of social control. The garrison handles bodies, the clergy handles minds, and both would prefer the other operated at lower volume.","category":"military","rawPower":19,"powerLabel":"Significant"},{"faction":"Town Council","modifier":null,"power":22,"desc":"An elected or appointed council governs; merchants, guilds, and prominent families compete for seats.","isGoverning":true,"category":"government","legitimacyCrisis":true,"crisisNote":"Governing authority is internally fractured. Real decisions are being made informally. The faction that appears to govern is not the faction that governs.","rawPower":34,"powerLabel":"Significant"},{"faction":"Religious Authorities","power":19,"desc":"Church holds substantial temporal power; tithes fund civic works and the clergy's opinion on appointments carries decisive weight. Genuinely three-way territory: no faction has decisively broken from the pack; every council vote is negotiated.","category":"religious","rawPower":17,"powerLabel":"Significant"},{"faction":"War Council","power":18,"desc":"Emergency committee with authority over rationing, conscription, and defence spending; not accountable to normal governance.","category":"military","rawPower":17,"powerLabel":"Significant"},{"faction":"Thieves' Guild","power":8,"desc":"Organised criminal network controls the black market and several informal revenue streams; present in council discussions through intermediaries. The garrison outweighs them institutionally. They survive by corrupting the lower ranks and making enforcement selectively unprofitable.","category":"criminal","rawPower":5,"powerLabel":"Suppressed"},{"faction":"Merchant Guilds","power":5,"desc":"Merchants with local reach; a consistent civic presence without yet being the dominant commercial voice. The craft guilds are close behind, contesting every pricing and quality-standard decision they try to push through council.","category":"economy","rawPower":3,"powerLabel":"Suppressed"},{"faction":"Craft Guilds","power":5,"desc":"Artisan guilds maintaining standards in a thin economy; not politically weak by choice, but by circumstance. Ahead of the merchant guilds in current influence: an unusual position they intend to hold.","category":"economy","rawPower":3,"powerLabel":"Suppressed"}],"governingName":"Town Council","government":"Town Council","stability":"Critical (active siege — survival priority)","recentConflict":"The settlement is under active siege. Every resource decision is a military decision. The debate is no longer about policy. It is about survival.","publicLegitimacy":{"score":2,"label":"Legitimacy Crisis","color":"#8b1a1a","bg":"#fdf4f4","breakdown":{"prosperity":-20,"safety":-20,"defense":0,"food":-8},"govMultiplier":0.6,"crimMultiplier":1.3,"isEndorsed":false,"isApproved":false,"isTolerated":false,"isContested":false,"isLegitimacyCrisis":true,"governanceFractured":true},"factionRelationships":[{"pair":["Town Council","Military/Guard"],"type":"tense","direction":"escalating","ratio":1.05,"narrative":"Military/Guard and Town Council hold roughly equal power. The commander's cooperation is sought, not commanded. Political decisions increasingly require military endorsement.","dmNote":null},{"pair":["Town Council","Merchant Guilds"],"type":"subordinate","direction":"stable","ratio":0.23,"narrative":"Merchant Guilds operates within the governance framework Town Council sets. Political access is purchased, not assumed."},{"pair":["Town Council","Religious Authorities"],"type":"dependent","direction":"stable","ratio":0.86,"narrative":"Town Council provides the sword; Religious Authorities provides the moral framework that makes taxation feel just and authority feel ordained. Each legitimises the other."},{"pair":["Town Council","Thieves' Guild"],"type":"competitive","direction":"escalating","captureState":"adversarial","narrative":"Town Council actively suppresses Thieves' Guild. Enforcement is genuine but incomplete. Thieves' Guild retreats and reorganises rather than disappearing.","dmNote":null},{"pair":["Merchant Guilds","Craft Guilds"],"type":"tense","direction":"stable","ratio":1,"narrative":"Merchant Guilds and Craft Guilds are structural allies against feudal extraction and structural rivals over value distribution. They vote together, then argue about the proceeds."},{"pair":["Thieves' Guild","Military/Guard"],"type":"competitive","direction":"escalating","captureState":"adversarial","narrative":"Military/Guard actively hunts Thieves' Guild. Arrests are real, enforcement is genuine. Thieves' Guild uses superior local knowledge and social embeddedness to absorb pressure and reconstitute."},{"pair":["Merchant Guilds","Religious Authorities"],"type":"dependent","direction":"stable","narrative":"Religious Authorities and Merchant Guilds sustain each other: church institutions provide charity that keeps social stability, merchants provide endowments that fund them. Neither is comfortable with the other's power."}],"criminalCaptureState":"adversarial","powerProjectionVersion":1,"economyInputFingerprint":"power-economy-v1:3fb98213","conflicts":[{"parties":["The Independent Bloc","The Shield Compact"],"issue":"Succession to a council seat","stakes":"Political influence","intensity":"low","desc":"The Independent Bloc and The Shield Compact are in low conflict over succession to a council seat. The stakes are political influence.","plotHooks":["A neutral figure is being pressured by both The Independent Bloc and The Shield Compact to take a side before the next council session.","Evidence has surfaced suggesting a third party is deliberately escalating the tension between the two factions.","Someone is offering to resolve the conflict \"permanently\" for a price. Both factions have received the offer. Neither has refused yet."]}]},"settlementReason":["A crossroads settlement. The meeting of routes is the whole of its fortune and the whole of its exposure."],"npcs":[{"id":"npc_1","name":"Vilbirg Werner","gender":"female","role":"Mayor","title":"Bürgermeister","category":"government","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"hypocritical","modifier":"cynical","tell":"maintains an unnervingly fixed smile during conflict","speech":"Prefaces bad news with elaborate courtesy, good news with none"},"physical":{"age":"mid-forties","build":"barrel-chested","feature":"a network of small scars on their knuckles","clothes":"expensive but conservative merchant dress"},"goal":{"short":"Restore enough perceived legitimacy to make the governing role functional, or identify an exit before the gap between title and authority becomes irreversible.","long":"Die in office having kept the peace (legacy matters more than wealth)"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["A recruit they turned away has since joined a different outfit. The different outfit is now paying them to monitor this one.","A merchant they publicly opposed is now publicly supporting them. No explanation offered."],"influence":"high","power":10,"presentation":{"impression":"Friendly and community-minded. The kind of person other residents speak well of.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Knows everyone, introduces you to people, seems like the natural first contact for newcomers."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Town Council","factionGoal":"Maintain Town Council's position against current pressure","structuralPosition":"Holds nominal governing authority where the legitimacy of that position is in active question. Formal title and real decision-making power are not the same thing.","activeConstraint":"Cannot take the action most likely to restore legitimacy without exposing the informal arrangements that currently keep governance functional.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_2","name":"Leopold Friedmann","gender":"male","role":"Guard Captain","title":"Hauptmann","category":"military","personality":{"dominant":"honest","flaw":"domineering","modifier":"detached","tell":"taps their foot in a complex rhythm when bored","speech":"Speaks in analogies and metaphors, even when clarity would serve better"},"physical":{"age":"mid-sixties","build":"imposingly tall","feature":"a cough they suppress with visible effort","clothes":"a dress uniform kept for funerals, worn thin at the elbows"},"goal":{"short":"Maintain operational cohesion and institutional loyalty while the political situation makes the chain of command ambiguous.","long":"Rebuild guard morale after years of under-funding and low prestige"},"secret":{"what":"Has been paying a health official to suppress a finding about their product","stakes":"People are being harmed; the official is growing nervous; the finding is documented"},"plotHooks":["A prisoner in their custody knows something valuable. So does someone with reason to ensure they never speak.","A weapons cache they were responsible for is smaller than it should be. They haven't reported it yet."],"influence":"high","power":9,"presentation":{"impression":"Efficient and correct in every interaction. The manner of someone following procedure.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Processes requests quickly. Doesn't ask about things that aren't their business."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Military/Guard","structuralPosition":"Commands enforcement capacity where civilian governance is failing. The military's relationship with civilian authority is under pressure.","activeConstraint":"Cannot act unilaterally to fill the governance vacuum without becoming a political actor in ways that compromise the institutional neutrality the role requires.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_4","name":"Adalbero Richter","gender":"male","role":"Garrison Commander","title":"Hauptmann","category":"military","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"cowardly","modifier":"iconoclast","tell":"takes written notes during conversations, even casual ones","speech":"Uses softening phrases that make every statement sound like a question"},"physical":{"age":"early thirties","build":"heavyset and solid","feature":"an old injury that affects their gait","clothes":"soldier's practical dress with officer's insignia"},"goal":{"short":"Maintain operational cohesion and institutional loyalty while the political situation makes the chain of command ambiguous.","long":"End this siege in a way the settlement can recover from"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["The ambush that killed two of their best people wasn't random. Someone knew the patrol route.","They are carrying out orders they believe are wrong. They have not yet decided at what point they stop carrying them out."],"influence":"high","power":10,"presentation":{"impression":"Warm, a little effusive. The first person to make you feel you've arrived somewhere safe.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Asks good questions about your journey. Remembers the answers."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Military/Guard","structuralPosition":"Commands enforcement capacity where civilian governance is failing. The military's relationship with civilian authority is under pressure.","activeConstraint":"Cannot act unilaterally to fill the governance vacuum without becoming a political actor in ways that compromise the institutional neutrality the role requires.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_3","name":"Gisela Schneider","gender":"female","role":"High Priest","title":"Pfarrer","category":"religious","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"imperious","modifier":"cautious","tell":"never volunteers information, only answers what is asked","speech":"Never interrupts, waits out even the longest speaker, then answers the first point only"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"barrel-chested","feature":"eyes that never stop moving","clothes":"plain devotional dress with one opulent accessory"},"goal":{"short":"Extend the institution's civic role in ways that survive whatever governance reconsolidation follows.","long":"Unite the fractious local clergy under a single doctrinal standard"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["A donation was made to the institution under conditions the donor didn't disclose publicly. The conditions are becoming relevant.","A novice has the gift. They know what that means for the novice. They're not sure what to do."],"influence":"moderate","power":5,"presentation":{"impression":"Watchful, in a religious way: not suspicious, but as though taking a reading.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","structuralPosition":"Holds institutional religious authority in a settlement where civic governance is failing. Religious institutions often absorb civic functions when secular authority contracts.","activeConstraint":"Civic engagement that appears opportunistic risks being reversed by a reconsolidated authority that resents the encroachment.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_5","name":"Nanthild Braun","gender":"female","role":"Guild Master","title":"Gildenmeister of Carriers'","category":"economy","personality":{"dominant":"humble","flaw":null,"modifier":"obsessive","tell":"refuses to sit with their back to a door","speech":"Deflects personal questions with philosophical tangents"},"physical":{"age":"late thirties","build":"slight: smaller than expected for the role","feature":"a ring on every finger","clothes":"last season's fashion maintained with visible determination"},"goal":{"short":"Prevent a rival guild from undercutting their members' prices","long":"Codify guild law so strongly that future masters can't easily corrupt it"},"secret":{"what":"Authorised an illegal sortie that failed. Five people died and no record was kept","stakes":"Vilbirg Werner survived it. They know, and they've been drinking heavily ever since"},"plotHooks":["They have been slowly acquiring a controlling interest in a competitor through intermediaries. The competitor hasn't noticed yet."],"influence":"low","power":3,"presentation":{"impression":"Busy, or presenting as busy. The first impression is of someone who doesn't waste time.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"institution":"Carriers' guild","corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_7","name":"Conrad Steiner","gender":"male","role":"Prophet/Seer","title":"Pfarrer","category":"religious","personality":{"dominant":"methodical","flaw":"imperious","modifier":"stoic","tell":"deflects personal questions with a counter-question","speech":"Refers to past events as though they're common knowledge"},"physical":{"age":"early fifties","build":"tall with a slight stoop","feature":"close-cropped hair","clothes":"ceremonial attire worn at all times"},"goal":{"short":"Identify the person inside the walls who is communicating with the besiegers","long":"End this siege in a way the settlement can recover from"},"secret":{"what":"Has agreed to hand over authority to an external power in exchange for personal safety","stakes":"Treason. Those they've sold out would not be forgiving"},"plotHooks":["They've noticed the same group of faces at multiple locations where incidents occurred. No one else has."],"influence":"low","power":3,"presentation":{"impression":"Watchful, in a religious way: not suspicious, but as though taking a reading.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_9","name":"Megingoz Klein","gender":"male","role":"Healer","title":"Heiler","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":"optimistic","flaw":"imperious","modifier":"ambitious","tell":"uses elaborate, florid greetings regardless of context","speech":"Uses understatement and dry humour as a defence mechanism"},"physical":{"age":"mid-thirties","build":"compact and powerful","feature":"a network of small scars on their knuckles","clothes":"travel-worn but well-maintained gear"},"goal":{"short":"Secure enough weapons reserves to outlast the blockade","long":"Survive this: everything else can wait"},"secret":{"what":"Owes Adalbero Richter a debt from before either of them held their current position: one that Adalbero Richter has never formally called in","stakes":"The silence feels like patience rather than forgiveness"},"plotHooks":["Someone is paying their soldiers more than their salary. The soldiers aren't saying who.","They received orders from above that contradict what they know to be right. They haven't acted on either yet."],"influence":"low","power":2,"presentation":{"impression":"Ordinary in a way that is itself a kind of presence.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_6","name":"Rudolf Koch","gender":"male","role":"Debt Collector","title":"Agent","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"cowardly","modifier":"cynical","tell":"makes deliberate, theatrical eye contact to assert dominance","speech":"Uses long pauses as punctuation, sits comfortably in silence"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"average height, unremarkable frame","feature":"eyes that never stop moving","clothes":"whatever was available (they don't care about dress)"},"goal":{"short":"Stay useful to the wrong people so they stay breathing.","long":"Matter to the people immediately around them: small scale, real"},"secret":{"what":"Is the illegitimate heir to a title currently held by someone who doesn't know they exist","stakes":"Could claim it, or could be seen as a threat by those who benefit from the status quo"},"plotHooks":["Someone left an item in their care and hasn't returned. The item is valuable. The absence is now suspicious.","They found something hidden in a place it shouldn't be. They put it back. They haven't told anyone."],"influence":"low","power":1,"presentation":{"impression":"Tired, but alert. The combination of someone who works hard and pays attention.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"corrupt":true,"corruptionVector":"fear","secondaryAffiliation":"Front businesses","corruptTies":{"criminalInstitution":"Front businesses","thievesGuild":"Front businesses"},"factionAffiliation":"War Council"},{"id":"npc_8","name":"Gunter Lange","gender":"male","role":"Master Builder","title":"Meister","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":"principled","flaw":"self-serving","modifier":"zealous","tell":"always stands when others sit, or vice versa","speech":"Addresses strangers formally and familiars by diminutives"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"compact and powerful","feature":"eyes that are slightly different colours","clothes":"clothes practical for their work with one personal flourish"},"goal":{"short":"Figure out what is actually going on before it affects them directly","long":"Matter to the people immediately around them: small scale, real"},"secret":{"what":"Has been skimming from the weapons reserves to pay a personal debt that predates the siege","stakes":"The shortage will be noticed when the final accounting is done. They're hoping they die before that happens"},"plotHooks":["They've been offered money to not ask questions about something they hadn't even started asking about.","Something they were told was destroyed is apparently not destroyed."],"influence":"low","power":2,"presentation":{"impression":"Reserved. Not hostile, just private.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Merchant Guilds","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"}],"relationships":[{"type":"political","typeName":"Jurisdictional Tension","description":"Vilbirg Werner issues orders Leopold Friedmann regards as suggestions, and Leopold Friedmann takes actions Vilbirg Werner regards as insubordination; the settlement runs in the gap between.","tension":"An incident is coming that will force the issue. Both are positioning for it.","strength":"convenience","npc1Id":"npc_1","npc2Id":"npc_2","npc1Name":"Vilbirg Werner","npc2Name":"Leopold Friedmann","npc1Role":"Mayor","npc2Role":"Guard Captain","archetypeKey":"gov_mil_friction","flagDriven":false},{"type":"respect","typeName":"Genuine Respect","description":"Vilbirg Werner and Adalbero Richter have earned each other's regard through demonstrated competence. They don't agree on everything but they trust each other's judgment within their respective domains.","tension":"One of them is being pressured to act against the other, and has not yet mentioned it.","strength":"genuine","npc1Id":"npc_1","npc2Id":"npc_4","npc1Name":"Vilbirg Werner","npc2Name":"Adalbero Richter","npc1Role":"Mayor","npc2Role":"Garrison Commander","archetypeKey":"genuine_respect","flagDriven":false},{"type":"mentor_student","typeName":"Mentor and Successor","description":"What Gisela Schneider knows, Vilbirg Werner taught (including, inconveniently, how to outmanoeuvre a teacher).","tension":"Gisela Schneider now operates in ways Vilbirg Werner would not approve of. Neither discusses the divergence directly.","strength":"lifelong","npc1Id":"npc_1","npc2Id":"npc_3","npc1Name":"Vilbirg Werner","npc2Name":"Gisela Schneider","npc1Role":"Mayor","npc2Role":"High Priest","archetypeKey":"mentor_legacy","flagDriven":false},{"type":"enemy","typeName":"Unresolved History","description":"The quarrel between Leopold Friedmann and Adalbero Richter is old enough that no one else remembers the cause. They remember. They have simply stopped explaining.","tension":"The circumstances that caused the original rupture are repeating. Both of them know it.","strength":"serious","npc1Id":"npc_2","npc2Id":"npc_4","npc1Name":"Leopold Friedmann","npc2Name":"Adalbero Richter","npc1Role":"Guard Captain","npc2Role":"Garrison Commander","archetypeKey":"bitter_history","flagDriven":false},{"type":"rival","typeName":"Professional Rivalry","description":"Every advance Gisela Schneider makes is answered by Conrad Steiner within the season; the rivalry has become its own institution, with rules neither wrote and both obey.","tension":"A decision coming in the next season will advantage one significantly. The other knows this.","strength":"personal","npc1Id":"npc_3","npc2Id":"npc_7","npc1Name":"Gisela Schneider","npc2Name":"Conrad Steiner","npc1Role":"High Priest","npc2Role":"Prophet/Seer","archetypeKey":"peer_rivalry","flagDriven":false},{"type":"mentor_student","typeName":"Mentor and Successor","description":"Gunter Lange stands where Gisela Schneider put them, by a ladder Gisela Schneider built and Gunter Lange has since pulled up. Both remember it differently.","tension":"Gunter Lange now operates in ways Gisela Schneider would not approve of. Neither discusses the divergence directly.","strength":"formal","npc1Id":"npc_3","npc2Id":"npc_8","npc1Name":"Gisela Schneider","npc2Name":"Gunter Lange","npc1Role":"High Priest","npc2Role":"Master Builder","archetypeKey":"mentor_legacy","flagDriven":false},{"type":"debtor_creditor","typeName":"Outstanding Debt","description":"Years ago Gisela Schneider did for Adalbero Richter the kind of favour that cannot be repaid, only serviced. Adalbero Richter has been servicing it ever since.","tension":"Gisela Schneider is about to call it in.","strength":"crushing","npc1Id":"npc_4","npc2Id":"npc_3","npc1Name":"Adalbero Richter","npc2Name":"Gisela Schneider","npc1Role":"Garrison Commander","npc2Role":"High Priest","archetypeKey":"old_debt","flagDriven":false},{"type":"debtor_creditor","typeName":"Outstanding Debt","description":"Years ago Nanthild Braun did for Adalbero Richter the kind of favour that cannot be repaid, only serviced. Adalbero Richter has been servicing it ever since.","tension":"A third party has learned what the original favour was. The debt just changed hands.","strength":"crushing","npc1Id":"npc_4","npc2Id":"npc_5","npc1Name":"Adalbero Richter","npc2Name":"Nanthild Braun","npc1Role":"Garrison Commander","npc2Role":"Guild Master","archetypeKey":"old_debt","flagDriven":false},{"type":"debtor_creditor","typeName":"Outstanding Debt","description":"Years ago Vilbirg Werner did for Nanthild Braun the kind of favour that cannot be repaid, only serviced. Nanthild Braun has been servicing it ever since.","tension":"A third party has learned what the original favour was. The debt just changed hands.","strength":"minor","npc1Id":"npc_5","npc2Id":"npc_1","npc1Name":"Nanthild Braun","npc2Name":"Vilbirg Werner","npc1Role":"Guild Master","npc2Role":"Mayor","archetypeKey":"old_debt","flagDriven":false},{"type":"respect","typeName":"Genuine Respect","description":"Nanthild Braun and Conrad Steiner disagree often and trust completely. Each has watched the other be right at cost, and neither forgets it.","tension":"They are about to be on opposite sides of a significant decision.","strength":"genuine","npc1Id":"npc_5","npc2Id":"npc_7","npc1Name":"Nanthild Braun","npc2Name":"Conrad Steiner","npc1Role":"Guild Master","npc2Role":"Prophet/Seer","archetypeKey":"genuine_respect","flagDriven":false},{"type":"ally","typeName":"Pragmatic Alliance","description":"Nanthild Braun and Gunter Lange are allies by arithmetic: each has counted the cost of the other as an enemy and found it too high. The friendship is warm, public, and entirely conditional.","tension":"Nanthild Braun has taken a precaution against Gunter Lange that Gunter Lange was not meant to discover. Gunter Lange has discovered it.","strength":"weak","npc1Id":"npc_5","npc2Id":"npc_8","npc1Name":"Nanthild Braun","npc2Name":"Gunter Lange","npc1Role":"Guild Master","npc2Role":"Master Builder","archetypeKey":"wary_alliance","flagDriven":false},{"type":"family","typeName":"Family Complication","description":"Rudolf Koch and Gunter Lange share a family and avoid sharing anything else; every professional dealing between them is conducted as though the relation were a rumour.","tension":"An inheritance, title, or secret is about to make the connection impossible to ignore.","strength":"close","npc1Id":"npc_6","npc2Id":"npc_8","npc1Name":"Rudolf Koch","npc2Name":"Gunter Lange","npc1Role":"Debt Collector","npc2Role":"Master Builder","archetypeKey":"family_complication","flagDriven":false},{"type":"mentor_student","typeName":"Mentor and Successor","description":"Megingoz Klein stands where Rudolf Koch put them, by a ladder Rudolf Koch built and Megingoz Klein has since pulled up. Both remember it differently.","tension":"Megingoz Klein now operates in ways Rudolf Koch would not approve of. Neither discusses the divergence directly.","strength":"devoted","npc1Id":"npc_6","npc2Id":"npc_9","npc1Name":"Rudolf Koch","npc2Name":"Megingoz Klein","npc1Role":"Debt Collector","npc2Role":"Healer","archetypeKey":"mentor_legacy","flagDriven":false},{"type":"ally","typeName":"Pragmatic Alliance","description":"Rudolf Koch and Nanthild Braun work together because the alternative (working against each other) is worse for both. The alliance holds as long as the calculation holds.","tension":"The threat that made the alliance necessary is gone. Neither has said so aloud.","strength":"moderate","npc1Id":"npc_6","npc2Id":"npc_5","npc1Name":"Rudolf Koch","npc2Name":"Nanthild Braun","npc1Role":"Debt Collector","npc2Role":"Guild Master","archetypeKey":"wary_alliance","flagDriven":false},{"type":"mentor_student","typeName":"Mentor and Successor","description":"What Vilbirg Werner knows, Conrad Steiner taught (including, inconveniently, how to outmanoeuvre a teacher).","tension":"Conrad Steiner has one favour left to call in, and is saving it. Vilbirg Werner knows, and is watching for it.","strength":"formal","npc1Id":"npc_7","npc2Id":"npc_1","npc1Name":"Conrad Steiner","npc2Name":"Vilbirg Werner","npc1Role":"Prophet/Seer","npc2Role":"Mayor","archetypeKey":"mentor_legacy","flagDriven":false},{"type":"ally","typeName":"Pragmatic Alliance","description":"Conrad Steiner and Gunter Lange work together because the alternative (working against each other) is worse for both. The alliance holds as long as the calculation holds.","tension":"Conrad Steiner has taken a precaution against Gunter Lange that Gunter Lange was not meant to discover. Gunter Lange has discovered it.","strength":"weak","npc1Id":"npc_7","npc2Id":"npc_8","npc1Name":"Conrad Steiner","npc2Name":"Gunter Lange","npc1Role":"Prophet/Seer","npc2Role":"Master Builder","archetypeKey":"wary_alliance","flagDriven":false},{"type":"political","typeName":"Mutual Leverage","description":"Gunter Lange and Megingoz Klein each hold information or resources the other needs. They cooperate efficiently and neither trusts the other at all.","tension":"Megingoz Klein has recently secured something that makes Gunter Lange's hold obsolete. The politeness continues, for now.","strength":"unbreakable","npc1Id":"npc_8","npc2Id":"npc_9","npc1Name":"Gunter Lange","npc2Name":"Megingoz Klein","npc1Role":"Master Builder","npc2Role":"Healer","archetypeKey":"mutual_leverage","flagDriven":false},{"type":"debtor_creditor","typeName":"Outstanding Debt","description":"Years ago Leopold Friedmann did for Gunter Lange the kind of favour that cannot be repaid, only serviced. Gunter Lange has been servicing it ever since.","tension":"A third party has learned what the original favour was. The debt just changed hands.","strength":"crushing","npc1Id":"npc_8","npc2Id":"npc_2","npc1Name":"Gunter Lange","npc2Name":"Leopold Friedmann","npc1Role":"Master Builder","npc2Role":"Guard Captain","archetypeKey":"old_debt","flagDriven":false},{"type":"ally","typeName":"Pragmatic Alliance","description":"Megingoz Klein and Nanthild Braun work together because the alternative (working against each other) is worse for both. The alliance holds as long as the calculation holds.","tension":"Megingoz Klein has taken a precaution against Nanthild Braun that Nanthild Braun was not meant to discover. Nanthild Braun has discovered it.","strength":"moderate","npc1Id":"npc_9","npc2Id":"npc_5","npc1Name":"Megingoz Klein","npc2Name":"Nanthild Braun","npc1Role":"Healer","npc2Role":"Guild Master","archetypeKey":"wary_alliance","flagDriven":false},{"type":"mentor_student","typeName":"Mentor and Successor","description":"Vilbirg Werner stands where Megingoz Klein put them, by a ladder Megingoz Klein built and Vilbirg Werner has since pulled up. Both remember it differently.","tension":"A third party has asked Megingoz Klein, quietly, whether Vilbirg Werner can be trusted. The answer took too long.","strength":"formal","npc1Id":"npc_9","npc2Id":"npc_1","npc1Name":"Megingoz Klein","npc2Name":"Vilbirg Werner","npc1Role":"Healer","npc2Role":"Mayor","archetypeKey":"mentor_legacy","flagDriven":false},{"type":"respect","typeName":"Genuine Respect","description":"There is no arrangement between Megingoz Klein and Conrad Steiner, only a long record of kept words; in this settlement that makes them remarkable.","tension":"They are about to be on opposite sides of a significant decision.","strength":"genuine","npc1Id":"npc_9","npc2Id":"npc_7","npc1Name":"Megingoz Klein","npc2Name":"Conrad Steiner","npc1Role":"Healer","npc2Role":"Prophet/Seer","archetypeKey":"genuine_respect","flagDriven":false}],"factions":[{"name":"The Independent Bloc","members":[{"id":"npc_5","name":"Nanthild Braun","gender":"female","role":"Guild Master","title":"Gildenmeister of Carriers'","category":"economy","personality":{"dominant":"humble","flaw":null,"modifier":"obsessive","tell":"refuses to sit with their back to a door","speech":"Deflects personal questions with philosophical tangents"},"physical":{"age":"late thirties","build":"slight: smaller than expected for the role","feature":"a ring on every finger","clothes":"last season's fashion maintained with visible determination"},"goal":{"short":"Prevent a rival guild from undercutting their members' prices","long":"Codify guild law so strongly that future masters can't easily corrupt it"},"secret":{"what":"Authorised an illegal sortie that failed. Five people died and no record was kept","stakes":"Vilbirg Werner survived it. They know, and they've been drinking heavily ever since"},"plotHooks":["They have been slowly acquiring a controlling interest in a competitor through intermediaries. The competitor hasn't noticed yet."],"influence":"low","power":3,"presentation":{"impression":"Busy, or presenting as busy. The first impression is of someone who doesn't waste time.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"institution":"Carriers' guild","corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_7","name":"Conrad Steiner","gender":"male","role":"Prophet/Seer","title":"Pfarrer","category":"religious","personality":{"dominant":"methodical","flaw":"imperious","modifier":"stoic","tell":"deflects personal questions with a counter-question","speech":"Refers to past events as though they're common knowledge"},"physical":{"age":"early fifties","build":"tall with a slight stoop","feature":"close-cropped hair","clothes":"ceremonial attire worn at all times"},"goal":{"short":"Identify the person inside the walls who is communicating with the besiegers","long":"End this siege in a way the settlement can recover from"},"secret":{"what":"Has agreed to hand over authority to an external power in exchange for personal safety","stakes":"Treason. Those they've sold out would not be forgiving"},"plotHooks":["They've noticed the same group of faces at multiple locations where incidents occurred. No one else has."],"influence":"low","power":3,"presentation":{"impression":"Watchful, in a religious way: not suspicious, but as though taking a reading.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_8","name":"Gunter Lange","gender":"male","role":"Master Builder","title":"Meister","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":"principled","flaw":"self-serving","modifier":"zealous","tell":"always stands when others sit, or vice versa","speech":"Addresses strangers formally and familiars by diminutives"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"compact and powerful","feature":"eyes that are slightly different colours","clothes":"clothes practical for their work with one personal flourish"},"goal":{"short":"Figure out what is actually going on before it affects them directly","long":"Matter to the people immediately around them: small scale, real"},"secret":{"what":"Has been skimming from the weapons reserves to pay a personal debt that predates the siege","stakes":"The shortage will be noticed when the final accounting is done. They're hoping they die before that happens"},"plotHooks":["They've been offered money to not ask questions about something they hadn't even started asking about.","Something they were told was destroyed is apparently not destroyed."],"influence":"low","power":2,"presentation":{"impression":"Reserved. Not hostile, just private.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Merchant Guilds","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"},{"id":"npc_6","name":"Rudolf Koch","gender":"male","role":"Debt Collector","title":"Agent","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"cowardly","modifier":"cynical","tell":"makes deliberate, theatrical eye contact to assert dominance","speech":"Uses long pauses as punctuation, sits comfortably in silence"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"average height, unremarkable frame","feature":"eyes that never stop moving","clothes":"whatever was available (they don't care about dress)"},"goal":{"short":"Stay useful to the wrong people so they stay breathing.","long":"Matter to the people immediately around them: small scale, real"},"secret":{"what":"Is the illegitimate heir to a title currently held by someone who doesn't know they exist","stakes":"Could claim it, or could be seen as a threat by those who benefit from the status quo"},"plotHooks":["Someone left an item in their care and hasn't returned. The item is valuable. The absence is now suspicious.","They found something hidden in a place it shouldn't be. They put it back. They haven't told anyone."],"influence":"low","power":1,"presentation":{"impression":"Tired, but alert. The combination of someone who works hard and pays attention.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"corrupt":true,"corruptionVector":"fear","secondaryAffiliation":"Front businesses","corruptTies":{"criminalInstitution":"Front businesses","thievesGuild":"Front businesses"},"factionAffiliation":"War Council"},{"id":"npc_9","name":"Megingoz Klein","gender":"male","role":"Healer","title":"Heiler","category":"other","personality":{"dominant":"optimistic","flaw":"imperious","modifier":"ambitious","tell":"uses elaborate, florid greetings regardless of context","speech":"Uses understatement and dry humour as a defence mechanism"},"physical":{"age":"mid-thirties","build":"compact and powerful","feature":"a network of small scars on their knuckles","clothes":"travel-worn but well-maintained gear"},"goal":{"short":"Secure enough weapons reserves to outlast the blockade","long":"Survive this: everything else can wait"},"secret":{"what":"Owes Adalbero Richter a debt from before either of them held their current position: one that Adalbero Richter has never formally called in","stakes":"The silence feels like patience rather than forgiveness"},"plotHooks":["Someone is paying their soldiers more than their salary. The soldiers aren't saying who.","They received orders from above that contradict what they know to be right. They haven't acted on either yet."],"influence":"low","power":2,"presentation":{"impression":"Ordinary in a way that is itself a kind of presence.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Cooperative within clear limits; every exchange has an implicit value."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","secondaryAffiliation":"Thieves' Guild"}],"dominantCategory":"other","powerFactionName":"Town Council","powerFactionPower":22,"powerFactionCat":"government"},{"name":"The Shield Compact","members":[{"id":"npc_1","name":"Vilbirg Werner","gender":"female","role":"Mayor","title":"Bürgermeister","category":"government","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"hypocritical","modifier":"cynical","tell":"maintains an unnervingly fixed smile during conflict","speech":"Prefaces bad news with elaborate courtesy, good news with none"},"physical":{"age":"mid-forties","build":"barrel-chested","feature":"a network of small scars on their knuckles","clothes":"expensive but conservative merchant dress"},"goal":{"short":"Restore enough perceived legitimacy to make the governing role functional, or identify an exit before the gap between title and authority becomes irreversible.","long":"Die in office having kept the peace (legacy matters more than wealth)"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["A recruit they turned away has since joined a different outfit. The different outfit is now paying them to monitor this one.","A merchant they publicly opposed is now publicly supporting them. No explanation offered."],"influence":"high","power":10,"presentation":{"impression":"Friendly and community-minded. The kind of person other residents speak well of.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Knows everyone, introduces you to people, seems like the natural first contact for newcomers."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Town Council","factionGoal":"Maintain Town Council's position against current pressure","structuralPosition":"Holds nominal governing authority where the legitimacy of that position is in active question. Formal title and real decision-making power are not the same thing.","activeConstraint":"Cannot take the action most likely to restore legitimacy without exposing the informal arrangements that currently keep governance functional.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_2","name":"Leopold Friedmann","gender":"male","role":"Guard Captain","title":"Hauptmann","category":"military","personality":{"dominant":"honest","flaw":"domineering","modifier":"detached","tell":"taps their foot in a complex rhythm when bored","speech":"Speaks in analogies and metaphors, even when clarity would serve better"},"physical":{"age":"mid-sixties","build":"imposingly tall","feature":"a cough they suppress with visible effort","clothes":"a dress uniform kept for funerals, worn thin at the elbows"},"goal":{"short":"Maintain operational cohesion and institutional loyalty while the political situation makes the chain of command ambiguous.","long":"Rebuild guard morale after years of under-funding and low prestige"},"secret":{"what":"Has been paying a health official to suppress a finding about their product","stakes":"People are being harmed; the official is growing nervous; the finding is documented"},"plotHooks":["A prisoner in their custody knows something valuable. So does someone with reason to ensure they never speak.","A weapons cache they were responsible for is smaller than it should be. They haven't reported it yet."],"influence":"high","power":9,"presentation":{"impression":"Efficient and correct in every interaction. The manner of someone following procedure.","disposition":"transactional","behaviour":"Processes requests quickly. Doesn't ask about things that aren't their business."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Military/Guard","structuralPosition":"Commands enforcement capacity where civilian governance is failing. The military's relationship with civilian authority is under pressure.","activeConstraint":"Cannot act unilaterally to fill the governance vacuum without becoming a political actor in ways that compromise the institutional neutrality the role requires.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"},{"id":"npc_4","name":"Adalbero Richter","gender":"male","role":"Garrison Commander","title":"Hauptmann","category":"military","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"cowardly","modifier":"iconoclast","tell":"takes written notes during conversations, even casual ones","speech":"Uses softening phrases that make every statement sound like a question"},"physical":{"age":"early thirties","build":"heavyset and solid","feature":"an old injury that affects their gait","clothes":"soldier's practical dress with officer's insignia"},"goal":{"short":"Maintain operational cohesion and institutional loyalty while the political situation makes the chain of command ambiguous.","long":"End this siege in a way the settlement can recover from"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["The ambush that killed two of their best people wasn't random. Someone knew the patrol route.","They are carrying out orders they believe are wrong. They have not yet decided at what point they stop carrying them out."],"influence":"high","power":10,"presentation":{"impression":"Warm, a little effusive. The first person to make you feel you've arrived somewhere safe.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Asks good questions about your journey. Remembers the answers."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Military/Guard","structuralPosition":"Commands enforcement capacity where civilian governance is failing. The military's relationship with civilian authority is under pressure.","activeConstraint":"Cannot act unilaterally to fill the governance vacuum without becoming a political actor in ways that compromise the institutional neutrality the role requires.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"}],"dominantCategory":"military","powerFactionName":"Military/Guard","powerFactionPower":23,"powerFactionCat":"military"},{"name":"The Devout Circle","members":[{"id":"npc_3","name":"Gisela Schneider","gender":"female","role":"High Priest","title":"Pfarrer","category":"religious","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"imperious","modifier":"cautious","tell":"never volunteers information, only answers what is asked","speech":"Never interrupts, waits out even the longest speaker, then answers the first point only"},"physical":{"age":"late twenties","build":"barrel-chested","feature":"eyes that never stop moving","clothes":"plain devotional dress with one opulent accessory"},"goal":{"short":"Extend the institution's civic role in ways that survive whatever governance reconsolidation follows.","long":"Unite the fractious local clergy under a single doctrinal standard"},"secret":{"what":"Passed information about the settlement's water supply to someone outside the walls three weeks ago","stakes":"People have already died because of it; they've been living with that knowledge"},"plotHooks":["A donation was made to the institution under conditions the donor didn't disclose publicly. The conditions are becoming relevant.","A novice has the gift. They know what that means for the novice. They're not sure what to do."],"influence":"moderate","power":5,"presentation":{"impression":"Watchful, in a religious way: not suspicious, but as though taking a reading.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions without volunteering; watches who you talk to next."},"corrupt":false,"factionAffiliation":"Religious Authorities","structuralPosition":"Holds institutional religious authority in a settlement where civic governance is failing. Religious institutions often absorb civic functions when secular authority contracts.","activeConstraint":"Civic engagement that appears opportunistic risks being reversed by a reconsolidated authority that resents the encroachment.","settlementCondition":"governance_fractured","structuralRank":"dominant"}],"dominantCategory":"religious","powerFactionName":"Religious Authorities","powerFactionPower":19,"powerFactionCat":"religious"}],"conflicts":[{"parties":["The Independent Bloc","The Shield Compact"],"issue":"Succession to a council seat","stakes":"Political influence","intensity":"low","desc":"The Independent Bloc and The Shield Compact are in low conflict over succession to a council s